#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
ares - agent-resume (was asm, Agent Session Manager): find and resume past agent sessions

Index architecture:
  reindex → builds JSON index from local .jsonl files ($AGENT_RESUME_HOME/data/indexes/)
  resume  → refreshes the index entries whose transcript changed, then searches it
  tmux    → after a crash, puts back the tmux sessions and Claude sessions of the previous boot,
            read from agent-tracker's files ($AGENT_TRACKER_HOME/data/sessions/<uuid>/)

Commands:
  ares resume [OPTIONS] [KEYWORD...]   Find and resume a past Claude Code or Codex session
  ares tmux [--dry-run] [--all] [--no-iterm]   Restore the previous boot's tmux sessions
  ares reindex                         Re-index all sessions now

  ares --version                       Show version
  ares --help                          Show this help

`asm` is an alias of `ares` (a symlink), kept for a while after the rename (2026-11-07).
"""

